        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "When the employer determines that an employee has been over paid, it shall notify the employee of this fact and the reasons therefore. The employer shall arrange to recover such overpayment from the employee over the same period of time in which the employee was overpaid [e.g. an employee who was overpaid by $5.00 per pay period for six months shall refund the employer at the rate of $5.00 per pay period for six months] unless the employer and the employee agree to another arrangement. A repayment schedule requested by the employee shall not be unreasonably denied. The employer shall ensure that through said recoupment, the affected employee shall neither be advantaged nor disadvantaged regarding leave accruals, retirement calculations, or other employment benefits.",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
